cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "Laplace Demon: an honest predictor laboratory for finite universes"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "madnessbrainsbl"
repository-code: "https://github.com/madnessbrainsbl/Laplace_Demon"
url: "https://github.com/madnessbrainsbl/Laplace_Demon"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-17"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free desktop laboratory that executes the Laplace's demon
  thought experiment honestly: exact prediction and retrodiction in finite
  cellular universes, law inference from observed events, measured Lyapunov
  horizons, a quantum kernel with decoherence and a CHSH Bell test, the
  information-theoretic Laplace coefficient L = I(E;K)/H(E), active-inference
  knowledge foraging, and executable demonstrations of the Bekenstein,
  Landauer, Godel/Wolpert and computational-irreducibility limits — plus a
  game in which a human observer loses to determinism.
keywords:
  - laplace-demon
  - determinism
  - cellular-automata
  - information-theory
  - quantum-mechanics
  - bell-inequality
  - chaos-theory
  - active-inference
  - thermodynamics-of-information
  - philosophy-of-science
